//
// Doc 31 increment R1 operator gate: ffn_resident, the one-segment resident
// FFN interior.
//
// Up-projection, GeLU and the J7b accumulator ring as three herds of ONE
// segment for a 64-row band: hidden arrives row-major and the shim's 4-D
// read pattern retiles it (seam 1); the finished H groups leave the up herd
// core->core to the GeLU herd in exactly the down ring's K order (seam 3)
// and fan through a memtile because a down core's two S2MM ports are spoken
// for. The [seq, ffn] interior -- ffn_up and ffn_gelu in the packaged
// tail's vocabulary -- crosses DRAM nowhere.
//
// Three arms, because the claim has three parts no single check can see:
//
// 1. STRUCTURE, first because it is host-only and fails fast: one
//    tile-bearing aie.device, core->core flows exactly herd_x, the shim
//    column budget, zero packet-typed channels, the down ring's 4 -> 2
//    hoist inside the composition, the three kernels dispatched by name.
//    A composition that re-split into segments or re-routed a hand-off
//    through L3 computes identical numbers, invisible below.
// 2. NUMBERS, on real NPU2: opcheck.py against the FP32 reference (the
//    same oracle as `ffn`), full-output np.isclose, zero mismatches.
// 3. The NEGATIVE CONTROL: hidden's (0, 0) perturbed after the reference
//    is computed, and the comparison must reject the run.
//
// NPU serialization lives one layer down: XRTRunner.run_test holds
// /tmp/npu.lock across load and dispatch. Taking the outer
// /tmp/mlir-air-npu.lock here would DEADLOCK against the gate command that
// invokes this suite.
//
// PARKED `[2026-08-11]`: every arm below compiles the module through aircc,
// and air-fuse-channels SEGVs on it NONDETERMINISTICALLY (use-after-free
// profile in the NFL merge path; minimal shape and boundary measured by
// agents/probes/probe_fuse_channels_sibling_nests.py -- 2 sibling
// same-bounds channel nests fuse, 3 crash). A gate that is an ASLR coin
// toss would flake the shared suite, so this recipe is UNSUPPORTED until
// the compiler fix lands; doc 31 "R1's gate is BLOCKED" carries the full
// report. Delete the UNSUPPORTED line -- and nothing else -- to arm it.
// UNSUPPORTED: true
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_npu2_ffn_resident_peano
// RUN: cd test_npu2_ffn_resident_peano
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile clean
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile check-ffn-resident-structure | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=STRUCT
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile check-ffn-resident PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR | FileCheck %s
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile check-ffn-resident-fault PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FAULT
//
// The device count, flow count and hoist count are stated inside the
// verdict line, so a lowering that re-split the segment, moved a stage
// edge, or kept the C pair in the K loop cannot match here; the script
// itself fails vacuous zeros (dumps present, channels present by name).
// STRUCT: [ffn-resident-structure] ffn_resident [64x3072x768]: PASS (1 device, 4 core->core, K-loop 4 -> 2, 0 packet-typed
// STRUCT: [ffn-resident-structure] PASS
//
// Both lines, not just the verdict: the first is XRTRunner's own, the
// second names the operator and shape, so a test wired to the wrong
// operator fails here rather than passing quietly.
// CHECK: PASS!
// CHECK: [opcheck] ffn_resident [64x3072x768]: PASS
//
// The injection line first: it names the element and both values. (0, 0)
// of the ROW-MAJOR hidden needs no packing arithmetic to interpret.
// FAULT: [fault-inject] input 0 at (0, 0)
// FAULT: [opcheck] ffn_resident [64x3072x768]: FAIL
// FAULT: NEGATIVE CONTROL: PASS
